  "worked_solution": "From the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n{28}^{∘}+(3x+{5}^{∘})={90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{28}^{∘}+(3x+{5}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 3x+{33}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & ={57}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={19}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
